  "query_preview": "/Monday through Friday/...\nIssued 345 AM MDT FRI JUL 24 2026\nCome Monday, the upper trough over the northwest coast will keep our \narea under a southwesterly flow on the dry side. Tuesday through the \nend of the week will generally see the return of hotter conditions, \nas the strong high pressure ridge off the Great Basin builds back in \nover the entire western CONUS. This ridging pattern will still allow \nsome monsoonal moisture to reach south-central Idaho around midweek, \nfavoring a slight chance of afternoon thunderstorms mainly near the \nMagic Valley and the Idaho-Nevada border. Otherwise, areas will \ngenerally be warm, dry, and breezy throughout the extended\nforecast.",
